From: Simon Polack <spolack+git@mailbox.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net: core: prefetch both lines of the next cached skb head

The build clears the head up to tail (two 128-byte lines) and the receive path reads the hash and the header fields of the second line back (opip_poll_skb: 0.6 L1 misses per packet at that read on the P2 image). Prefetch the second line of the next cached head too.

Signed-off-by: Simon Polack <spolack+git@mailbox.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/net/core/skbuff.c
+++ b/net/core/skbuff.c
@@ -309,9 +309,13 @@
 	}
 
 	skb = nc->skb_cache[--nc->skb_count];
-	/* The next one's first line, for the next build's clear and reads */
-	if (nc->skb_count)
-		prefetch(nc->skb_cache[nc->skb_count - 1]);
+	/* The next one's lines, for the next build's clear and reads */
+	if (nc->skb_count) {
+		struct sk_buff *next = nc->skb_cache[nc->skb_count - 1];
+
+		prefetch(next);
+		prefetch(&next->truesize);
+	}
 	local_unlock_nested_bh(&napi_alloc_cache.bh_lock);
 	kasan_mempool_unpoison_object(skb, kmem_cache_size(net_hotdata.skbuff_cache));
 
